{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/154990-sprits-as-familiar","id":154990,"title":"Sprits as Familiar?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-31T10:45:26-07:00","id":154990,"title":"Sprits as Familiar?","content":"Hi to all, just a quick question about spirits.<br /> There's a chance for a werewolf to tame a spirit and make it his own familiar? If yes, how many options there are?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T11:00:20-07:00","id":155005,"title":"","content":"Eh... you can add them to fetish' in a way or make allies of them, but I'm not sure you can get an exact familiar. What you'd wind up with would be something like a mini totem or contact. It would have to get something out of the whole deal. <br /> <br /> Example: You want to know if someone enters your empty field with a locus yes? You 'hire' a spirit nearby to watch it in exchange for free essence (for it). I can't think of a situation where a spirit will help you for free.<br /> <br /> I don't think you can &quot;tame&quot; a spirit either for that matter. They have a very alien thinking pattern to what we're used to in the mundane world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T11:52:54-07:00","id":155056,"title":"","content":"Nah there's no mechanics for getting a spirit familiar for werewolves.<br /> You could just use the mage or lucifuge hunter merit (it's for demons but mechanically could be used for spirits). I want to say promethean has one as well.<br /> <br /> I think the thing is, like totems, spirits can dampen their hostilities towards the Uratha, allowing for alliances. That's why every Uratha doesn't get ganked the moment they first step into Shadow, the spirit hatred for their kind is not a universal enmity. Whether it hangs around to feed on the result from your death rages or has some other incentive to keeping you around, or it's just something that aligns itself with the goal of the group, it has seemed like a possibility from the start that has never, as far as I know, been explored. It's one of the reasons we're happy for spirit packmates in Idigam chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-31-2014, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T13:01:55-07:00","id":155118,"title":"","content":"I never saw that 'spirit hatred' as belligerent as most people assume it to be. I always see it more in terms of xenophobia or racism, not crime against humanity prone hatred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T13:53:46-07:00","id":155197,"title":"","content":"Yes, like people vs the Authority. Most spirits don't stray out of line, but they do what they do and if they ever did anything different a wolf may see it as its duty to kill it. Or just because the wolf doesn't like what they do.<br /> <br /> But there's plenty of spirits that outright hate the Uratha, there's also a good amount that could be allied to them in a form other than being a totem or willing fetish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T16:59:16-07:00","id":155307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/154990-sprits-as-familiar?p=155056#post155056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah there's no mechanics for getting a spirit familiar for werewolves.<br /> You could just use the mage or lucifuge hunter merit (it's for demons but mechanically could be used for spirits). I want to say promethean has one as well.<br /> <br /> I think the thing is, like totems, spirits can dampen their hostilities towards the Uratha, allowing for alliances. That's why every Uratha doesn't get ganked the moment they first step into Shadow, the spirit hatred for their kind is not a universal enmity. Whether it hangs around to feed on the result from your death rages or has some other incentive to keeping you around, or it's just something that aligns itself with the goal of the group, it has seemed like a possibility from the start that has never, as far as I know, been explored. It's one of the reasons we're happy for spirit packmates in Idigam chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits have practical reasons for not liking the Uratha. For one, they're self-appointed furry cops with short fuses, they can do things that a spirit can't, and they have a mindset and life cycle that is completely beyond a spirit's understanding.<br /> <br /> Lastly, the most practical reasons for spirit to fear/hate the Death Rage in Uratha is the fact that it's much akin to a officer decked out in full SWAT armor high on PCP. Would you want to happen in your neighborhood?<br /> <br /> The thing that I always keep coming around to is that the spirits that tend to favor order and balance in the Shadow will tend to lean towards the Forsaken more than the Pure. Hell, I have had a spirit of City favor the Forsaken over the Pure because of the police-like attitude (Well, that and the Predator Kings blew up a few buildings that pissed it off).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 05-31-2014, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}